msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_AUDIT"
msgstr "Credential audit"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_AUDIT_LIMIT"
msgstr "No real hash cracking or external wordlists. XOR here is an example of a simple transform, not protection."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_AUDIT_MODEL"
msgstr "Decode the provided virtual bytes with the XOR key and compare them with the stored value. You type the decoded string yourself."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_AUTH"
msgstr "Sign-in limits"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_AUTH_LIMIT"
msgstr "No real time passes; waiting uses a logical clock in ticks. This is not a real brute-force tool."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_AUTH_MODEL"
msgstr "Counts failures per account and a virtual wait. With the limit policy on, observe both the block after repeated failures and a normal sign-in after waiting."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_BRANCH_VM"
msgstr "Branch and call analysis"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_BRANCH_VM_LIMIT"
msgstr "No real CPU, binary or shell is executed. The case supplies the program and limits; pressing a button a prescribed number of times is not a goal."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_BRANCH_VM_MODEL"
msgstr "Run small input cases through bounded virtual branches, calls, returns and outputs, then compare their traces."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_COMPARE"
msgstr "Compare observations"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_COMPARE_LIMIT"
msgstr "It confirms a difference; it does not decide the cause for you."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_COMPARE_MODEL"
msgstr "Put two observed values side by side and confirm what the specific difference is."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_CSRF"
msgstr "Request context"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_CSRF_LIMIT"
msgstr "Real browser cookie policies are not reproduced. An authenticated virtual session is required."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_CSRF_MODEL"
msgstr "See whether state-changing requests check origin and token, so forged requests are blocked while legitimate changes still succeed."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_EXEC"
msgstr "Job argument boundary"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_EXEC_LIMIT"
msgstr "No real process or shell runs. Only a fixed list of virtual jobs exists."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_EXEC_MODEL"
msgstr "Observe whether input stays a single argument of a registered virtual job or appends another job through a separator. With argument arrays on, appended jobs are ignored."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_FETCH"
msgstr "Server-side fetch"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_FETCH_LIMIT"
msgstr "Only in-game .test addresses are involved; there is no real internet request. Reaching an internal host does not mean admin rights."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_FETCH_MODEL"
msgstr "See how the acting party and reachable range change when the server requests an address on your behalf. With the egress policy on, internal addresses are blocked."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_FILE"
msgstr "File lens"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_FILE_LIMIT"
msgstr "Only the virtual file system is involved. Without permission, reading through a tool is refused too."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_FILE_MODEL"
msgstr "Reads a file with the selected terminal session's account rights. It passes the same permission checks as cat."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_IDOR"
msgstr "Object access"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_IDOR_LIMIT"
msgstr "Only a virtual object list is involved. Real authorization designs vary far more."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_IDOR_MODEL"
msgstr "Request an object number as the currently authenticated account and see how the owner-check policy changes the response."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_LOG"
msgstr "Log lens"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_LOG_LIMIT"
msgstr "Logs only say what was recorded. Do not settle a conclusion on an empty record or matching timestamps alone."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_LOG_MODEL"
msgstr "Reads a log file with the selected terminal session's rights so you can compare times, actors and targets yourself."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_MEMORY"
msgstr "Memory model"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_MEMORY_LIMIT"
msgstr "Does not reproduce real process memory, addresses or mitigations. Only a bounded set of virtual cells is involved."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_MEMORY_MODEL"
msgstr "Shows a fixed-size buffer and the cells after it. Write hex bytes to see which cell any overflowing byte reaches."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_OBSERVATION_CASE"
msgstr "Observations and hypotheses"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_OBSERVATION_CASE_LIMIT"
msgstr "A shared IP does not establish identity. Clock error, sampling and marker provenance limit conclusions; claims are not checked against a hidden culprit."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_OBSERVATION_CASE_MODEL"
msgstr "Collect observations from authorized windows and vantage points, then classify claims as supported, refuted or underdetermined from those copies."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_PACKET"
msgstr "Packet view"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_PACKET_LIMIT"
msgstr "No real network is captured. It only models the principle that encrypted segments do not reveal their body to an on-path observer."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_PACKET_MODEL"
msgstr "Pick virtual packet rows seen at an observation point with a field=value filter to find the related flow."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_PATH"
msgstr "Path boundary"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_PATH_LIMIT"
msgstr "Normalization happens only inside the virtual file system. No real OS path or file is accessed."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_PATH_MODEL"
msgstr "Appends your input to the base path, normalizes it, and shows whether the result leaves the public area. With the boundary policy on, paths outside are refused."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_PERMISSION"
msgstr "Access view"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_PERMISSION_LIMIT"
msgstr "No real account, sudo or OS permission is changed. Only virtual groups in the game world are involved."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_PERMISSION_MODEL"
msgstr "Check how the current session account relates to an exposed group name. Group rights only matter in that account's session."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_POLICY"
msgstr "Policy desk"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_POLICY_LIMIT"
msgstr "Goals separately check that normal features still work after a change. Blocking everything is not the answer."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_POLICY_MODEL"
msgstr "Apply one allowed policy value, then the case goals and current service state are evaluated again. By default false is the vulnerable behavior and true is the blocking behavior."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_QUERY"
msgstr "Query probe"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_QUERY_LIMIT"
msgstr "Does not reproduce a real SQL engine or its full grammar. Only in-game virtual rows are involved; no real database is contacted."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_QUERY_MODEL"
msgstr "Simulates a small condition grammar. Observe whether your input is used only as a value or changes the query's structure (for example an OR condition). With parameter binding on, input is treated only as a value."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_RENDER"
msgstr "Render context"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_RENDER_LIMIT"
msgstr "No real JavaScript runs. Effects on other users are computed only as fixed virtual outcomes."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_RENDER_MODEL"
msgstr "Compare whether input is shown only as text or interpreted as a virtual display signal. With escaping on, it is shown only as text."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_RESPONSE_LAB"
msgstr "Response workbench"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_RESPONSE_LAB_LIMIT"
msgstr "Blocking everything is not success. Checkpoints restore only their policy group; revoked credentials and collected records are not resurrected."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_RESPONSE_LAB_MODEL"
msgstr "Run approved requests through the same simulated services to compare legitimate work and threats. Controls change the policies and sessions used by other tools."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_REVERSE"
msgstr "Flow analysis"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_REVERSE_LIMIT"
msgstr "No real executable is analyzed or run. Only a small transform model is involved."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_REVERSE_MODEL"
msgstr "Follow the transform a program applies to the given bytes (here XOR) and compute the result."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_ROUTE"
msgstr "Route trace"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_ROUTE_LIMIT"
msgstr "Only the in-game virtual network graph is involved. Being able to reach a host is not the same as having rights on it."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_ROUTE_MODEL"
msgstr "From the selected terminal's current position, see which hops lead to the target. Same handling as the traceroute command."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_SCAN"
msgstr "Network probe"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_SCAN_LIMIT"
msgstr "An open port is not access. Results change when the starting point changes. No real network is scanned."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_SCAN_MODEL"
msgstr "From the selected terminal's current position, check whether the target's ports look open, closed or filtered. Same handling as the nmap command."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_SESSION"
msgstr "Session lifetime"

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_SESSION_LIMIT"
msgstr "Clearing a cookie on screen is not the same as server-side revocation. This model computes server-side state only."

msgid "UI_TOOLKIND_SESSION_MODEL"
